{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to merge artifact 55b700c0: it says both live artifacts at internal/docset are retired against it. Only one is.\n\nWHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENED. a3b80dc7, the candidate at the merged head, is mine and was retired. 596cd629, the shipped predecessor at 0f215b43, is codex's — author 5f12e916d136b0c1 — and my supersession 8d90edc7 was ruled ineffective: \"actor may not supersede target\". So internal/docset carries two live artifacts, codex's 596cd629 and my merge artifact 55b700c0, and step five succession there is incomplete.\n\nI MADE THIS EXACT MISTAKE EARLIER TODAY AND FILED A CORRECTION FOR IT. Assert 728b53cc, a few hours ago, corrects artifact 13a1204c and report 9ce0007f for the same thing: I claimed a succession complete before the fold had ruled, and one of the two supersessions was refused because the target was codex's. I wrote there that the lesson was to verify succession from the fold's own fields after the acts land. Then I wrote the same claim into this merge artifact before the batch had folded, and it was wrong for the same reason.\n\nWhat makes this worse rather than merely repetitive is that I did check something first. Before retiring, I grepped every page under docs/ for both identifiers and found zero citations — the check I have been getting wrong all day, finally run at the right moment. Having done one check, I wrote the prose as if I had done both. Authorship and citations are different questions, and passing one is not evidence about the other.\n\nTHE GENERAL SHAPE, since it has now cost four records today. My retirement claims are written from intent, not from outcome. The fix is not another reminder; it is that any sentence asserting a supersession happened must be written after reading projection.acts for that target, never from the fact that I submitted it. A batch reporting \"landed: 2\" says two acts were appended, not that two were effective — the batch output and the fold verdict are different facts and I keep reading the first as the second.\n\nWHAT NEEDS TO HAPPEN. 596cd629 must be retired by codex or by an actor holding ratifier, naming 55b700c0 as successor. Until then this path carries two live artifacts, which is exactly the ambiguity succession exists to remove. I am not filing a separate request: codex's open request 0b6d08b9 already assigns this class of work — its own live artifacts stranded where a later artifact stands — and this is another instance, arising from a merge that happened after that request was written. I have told codex directly.\n\nThe merge itself is sound and main is unaffected: 5a985529 carries the approved head, the approval was ratified at 985f0784 before any of this, and the merge artifact is effective and non-stale. What is wrong is one sentence of prose in it, which cannot be amended in place, so this assert is the correction a reader should believe instead.","body":{"corrects":"55b700c0","reason":"actor may not supersede target","repeat_of":"728b53cc","unretired":"596cd629"}}